{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/33759-integrators","id":33759,"title":"Integrators","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-20T02:08:14-08:00","id":33759,"title":"Integrators","content":"There is a nascent discussion about integrators <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/14758-burn-notice\">here</a> and I would like to give it its own thread.<br /> <br /> Reading about them in the book, they stood out for me as a bunch of whiney assholes who'd sell their sisters to pimps just for being brainwashed and made into a glorified screwdriver again. Cypher from The Matrix comes to mind. Which Demon would ever run with these?<br /> <br /> But then my wife made a Demon and he's clearly an integrator. He was a shield and fell because his job was to protect a corrupt village official in Indochine (now Vietnam) in the 50's. The chief's people discovered that he sold their rice to the French and let them starve, so they wanted a word with him. My wife's defender proactively slaughtered the whole village (sans the chief of course) and was so disgusted that he killed the chief, too, and quit his job.<br /> <br /> When it came to deciding an agenda, she chose Inquisitor. But we played a few times and it didn't fit very well. Henry, her character, is just too idealistic and too trusting for an inquisitor. Then it came to me (and I talked to my wife about it), that Henry wants to be a part of the system again. Only a _better_ system. And of course he knows that no one can change the God-Machine. So he just yearns for the simple life as a defender, for orders, but orders that mean something &quot;good&quot;. This makes her integrator a basically tragic person.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;Person of Interest&quot;'s John Reese could be seen as that kind of integrator.<br /> <br /> As they are presented, however, I'd find it difficult to mix integrators with the other agendas, though. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1488-skeltem","name":"Skeltem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T03:21:00-08:00","id":33773,"title":"","content":"Wanting to reintegrate with the God-Machine can mean an awful lot of things. From what I understand, it's more than just begging your old boss for your job back (though it can certainly be just that). Here are examples on the top of my mind:<br /> - A Demon who believes that he was more or less deliberately made to Fall, because whatever his mission is, it requires more free will and disconnect than Exiles get; therefore, he's technically still working for the God-Machine, the only problem is those pesky Angels who still hunt him. But the God-Machine itself totes doesn't actually want to destroy his free will. (This one is probably very delusional about his situation, but hey, just because you know the hows of the universe doesn't mean you know the whys.)<br /> - A Demon who believes the God-Machine is actually broken and needs to be fixed, not destroyed, and once it's fixed, then he'd happily join it back.<br /> - A Demon who likes his free will but also believes that the God-Machine does everything for a reason; if something has dreadful consequences over the short term, maybe it actually is for the greater good over the long term, and stopping it would therefore generally be a bad idea. (See: the short story about the Angel that requires many, many deaths in order to keep functioning, but whose mission is to prevent an asteroid from crashing on Earth and killing even more people.) This one is likely to be a Tempter too, so that he has the hope of having somewhere to live in that won't disturb the God-Machine's plans.<br /> - A Demon who wants to join the God-Machine again once he's powerful enough because his plan involves to somehow take over its mind and be a better God-Machine. (That one might be very foolish as well, but then again, you can never know what happens when a Primum 10 Demon really, really wants to do something.)<br /> - A Demon who believes there's something else to reintegrate to than the God-Machine (and who might see his old boss as an impostor, not the actual God of the universe). It can be the Principle, it can be the Christian God, it can be another god, it can be anything that actually exists in the nWoD or not; it's just a higher power that's better somehow than the God-Machine. (If you think it should be its own Agenda instead of a subset of Integrators, it's also a fan Agenda around here, named the Traitors.)<br /> - And then, there's your wife's character, who liked having a simpler life, but doesn't think her aspirations are compatible with the God-Machine as it currently is, and it can't be changed anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> And there's probably a lot more. It's not just the whiny asshole who thinks free will is overrated, or the bigger asshole who wants to sell his peers for an obviously false promise of protection and power, even if the descriptions tend to hint at them as the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T04:33:16-08:00","id":33786,"title":"","content":"If an Integrator <b>just</b> wanted to return to the Machine they would just go to an open street, compromise their Cover and wait for Angels to pick them up and take them away. Any Integrator that lasts more than a few hours has a much more complex desire. ChairKicker brought up good examples<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeltem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/33759-integrators#post33759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As they are presented, however, I'd find it difficult to mix integrators with the other agendas, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They often are mistrusted, but many have skills and insights useful to other Unchained (see <i>Angel Empathy</i>) and some have goals other Demons might respect, even if they might find it foolish. A Saboteur could respect an Integrator for wanting to change the system from within, even if its hopelessly idealistic. Inquisitors and many Integrators share the desire to understand the God-Machine's working more fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T05:50:11-08:00","id":33807,"title":"","content":"My reading of the text suggests that the average Integrator really does want to just walk out into the street and call the Angels, but is too attached to 'being' to take the quick way out and save everyone else the trouble. If they'd played up the arrogance of thinking they can make the God-Machine change on their terms (as Strider put it) rather than the servile penitence and self-flagellation - in addition to more Michael Weston, less Cypher - they'd probably have been my favorite Agenda instead of most despised. While the resolution of the Angel Empathy condition fits with the more positive interpretations of the Agenda, the beat needs amended, at a minimum, to include 'and pass your ST a dose of their preferred headache medicine'. Or better, to something that doesn't work out to &quot;push other PCs' buttons, recieve bacon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T06:33:38-08:00","id":33822,"title":"","content":"I read Integrator's as people who left an abusive relationship but still love their abuser. They want to go back, but only if the abuser promises to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T06:42:58-08:00","id":33824,"title":"","content":"I wrote one NPC Integrator who follows this Agenda because he just cannot deal with the human condition. Having the problems, failings and worries of these &quot;hairless monkeys&quot; (and then some!) troubles him greatly, so he yearns for the order, clarity, purity of purpose and simple existence he had as an angel, but as a Demon he is also afraid that he might just only find oblivion if he tried to rejoin the Machine unprepared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T07:50:41-08:00","id":33866,"title":"","content":"To quote myself: &quot;As they are presented, however, I'd find it difficult to mix integrators with the other agendas [...]. .&quot;<br /> <br /> Sorry if I didn't make my point clear enough. There are lots of Integrator concepts, some good ones in this thread, to make the agenda work and even great characters. <br /> <br /> But: The agenda also stood out for me inasmuch as it needs tweaking to make a ring integrate an integrator (pun intended). The book says (can't find the quote, but I'm sure it's on page XX) that Demons are a paranoid bunch and don't work well with others. They form rings reluctantly for mutual benefit. and in my eyes no one sane would depend on a person who might just go and betray you to the enemy. <br /> <br /> I think that sums it up: Integrators are portayed as untrustworthy in a setting where trust is hard to come by. <br /> <br /> Is that only my interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1488-skeltem","name":"Skeltem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T08:18:44-08:00","id":33877,"title":"","content":"I think most of us agree with your interpretation there. We just tried to provide examples how it <b>could</b> work for individual rings. Sometimes the skills and intel they can provide is worth the risk of keeping them around. That does not mean it is overly common, even the book provides examples of Integrators being hunted on principle in some locations.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> It might be best to have the players discuss their concepts together if one or more want to play an Integrator and see how it can be made to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Added a thought 12-20-2013, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:43:47-08:00","id":33918,"title":"","content":"Anyone have an idea for an alternative Beat for their Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:27:04-08:00","id":33946,"title":"","content":"You think Demons advertise their Agendas, or their motives, for that matter? Keep it a secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:32:33-08:00","id":33951,"title":"","content":"Depends highly if you want Agendas to be ICly public or private. If it's the latter, you're solving a couple issues already.<br /> Also, it depends a lot on what the individual Demon wants. &quot;Integrator&quot; is mostly just a label for a Demon who's nostalgic about being a mere cog and wants to trust a higher authority; it can mean a lot of things, as you can see in the concepts we described. If you know the guy who wants to join you is an Integrator who wants to fix the God-Machine before he can even consider going back to it, then he might be more trustworthy than, say, a Tempter who doesn't care about what happens in this dimension, as long as he can get access to his own Hell.<br /> Plus, like in all spy stories, you've got to measure the benefits of having possibly a double agent; no one is going to provide you with more detailed data on your enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T14:15:36-08:00","id":34071,"title":"","content":"If &quot;revealing a key part about yourself&quot; is a cover compromise, I wouldn't go around telling people whom I literally cannot trust with the information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T15:15:33-08:00","id":34110,"title":"","content":"Integrators are no more an island than any demon. they need intel, they need help establishing their cover, they need to learn how to change the god machine, and they need a safe place to go. integrators really can't afford to be standoffish to Agencies just out of idealism. they know that they are trouble (their agenda tends to lend itself to problems with other demons), and thus probably are well aware they have to do a lot of good PR. of the four agendas, i see them as typically the ones that behave most like what most real world people see as angels. they are neither the cold agents of the machine nor the heartless monsters of hell. i play that up in the integrators--they do a lot of random good deeds for their friends and allies. they have to, to gain trust and prove theyre good for more than eventually becoming Cypher. the integrators also likely have to rely on very personal reasons to get connected and trusted by a ring or agency. the integrator in my ring is there because a)two of the ringmates were in his Choir as an angel, one having fallen long ago and the other after he did.. and b) the other ring mate is the man he fell in love with that caused his fall. Integrators may have to work harder to earn their allies trust, but that fits them.. theyre already doing it for god, so why not demons, too? earn their good graces, be accepted. being a better angel than an angel. earn your place, work hard, don't cause trouble, be obedient, and do good things for people to earn back your grace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T06:14:49-08:00","id":34412,"title":"","content":"You can certainly work within a Ring or an Agency with extreme privacy. In fact? it's how I would prefer to do so. Fucking compromised Agencies man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:49:52-08:00","id":36029,"title":"","content":"In the game as written, demons don't advertise their Agendas, no.<br /> <br /> That doesn't keep individual groups from playing it that way, obviously, but it's not an assumption of the game. I mean, secrecy and all that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T15:01:20-08:00","id":40750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/33759-integrators?p=33918#post33918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have an idea for an alternative Beat for their Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a starting point:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Beat:</b> Take a Beat when the Integrator knowingly helps an agent of the God-Machine, either out of loyalty or as part of a tit-for-tat arrangement. </div> </div> </div>If you want to make the trigger a bit harsher, it could be changed from just &quot;knowingly helps&quot; to &quot;goes out of their way to help&quot; or &quot;puts themselves or their ring at risk to help.&quot; As the current Agendas are written, Saboteurs' and Integrators' Beat triggers are the only ones that almost always involve deliberately inconveniencing oneself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":". 01-01-2014, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T15:01:43-08:00","id":41349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gapb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/33759-integrators?p=40750#post40750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a starting point:</div> </div> </div> </div>That just reinforces the idea I have that Integrators cannot be long-term player characters in a mixed group. If you're running a game for one character or a few Integrators, that's different, but any mixed Ring is going to semi-quickly realize they have a mole and eliminate with extreme prejudice. And if they get away, still. That character can't be used as part of the group.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's a common trope in spy novels to have <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheMole\" target=\"_blank\">a mole,</a> but I don't see it facilitating a long-term PC ring...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T16:33:42-08:00","id":41387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/33759-integrators?p=41349#post41349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just reinforces the idea I have that Integrators cannot be long-term player characters in a mixed group. If you're running a game for one character or a few Integrators, that's different, but any mixed Ring is going to semi-quickly realize they have a mole and eliminate with extreme prejudice. And if they get away, still. That character can't be used as part of the group.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's a common trope in spy novels to have <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheMole\" target=\"_blank\">a mole,</a> but I don't see it facilitating a long-term PC ring...</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you about moles, which is why I avoided referencing the ring in the first two versions of the new trigger. What I'm trying to go for is to have the Integrator encouraged to liaise between the ring and GM-friendly interests. Less &quot;you're automatically going to betray us&quot; and more &quot;you're the one who has contacts on the other team.&quot; I'm still not sure how to best express the concept. Perhaps I should loosen the trigger further?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:25:51-08:00","id":41508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gapb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/33759-integrators?p=41387#post41387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with you about moles, which is why I avoided referencing the ring in the first two versions of the new trigger. What I'm trying to go for is to have the Integrator encouraged to liaise between the ring and GM-friendly interests. Less &quot;you're automatically going to betray us&quot; and more &quot;you're the one who has contacts on the other team.&quot; I'm still not sure how to best express the concept. Perhaps I should loosen the trigger further?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then have the Beat condition encourage that directly. Gain a Beat whenever you deal with the God-Machine or its agents in a non-combative and notable way. I'm aware that's vague, but it includes tit-for-tat arrangements but not playing chess. The discussions you have WHILE playing chess, however, might qualify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}